error[E0105]: an enum member's name goes right after the `.`
  --> tests/ui/enum_member_syntax.wid:11:13
   |
11 |   d: Dir = . North
   |             ^ remove this space
   = note: `.name` names a member of the enum expected here, like `.North`
help: remove the space
   |   d: Dir = .North
   = see `wid explain E0105`

error[E0105]: `.to_s` starts a line, so it calls a method on nothing
  --> tests/ui/enum_member_syntax.wid:13:3
   |
13 |   .to_s(2)
   |   ^^^^^ this call has no receiver
   = note: a line that starts with `.` continues the statement above only when it is indented deeper than the statement's first line, and the line above doesn't open a block; otherwise `.name` is an enum member
help: indent it deeper than the line above, to continue that line
   |     .to_s(2)
   = see `wid explain E0105`

